WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:07.320 align:start position:19%
There is a cruel irony in it.
A civilization that could predict

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:10.760 align:start position:19%
eclipses to the exact day could not
predict the rain.

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:16.040 align:start position:19%
All their astronomy, all their
mathematics, and the one cycle that

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:20.160 align:start position:19%
truly mattered slipped right past them.
It makes you wonder what we are missing

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:26.000 align:start position:19%
right now. And here is what most people
get wrong. The Maya never disappeared.

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:30.640 align:start position:19%
Standing here a thousand years ago, you
would see farmers, scribes, and kings

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:34.560 align:start position:19%
going about their day.
Today, their descendants number in the

00:00:32.599 --> 00:00:42.120 align:start position:19%
millions, still speaking Mayan
languages, still farming the same land.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:42.120 align:start position:19%
The cities fell. The people endured.

